AmiAirPrint 1.2
================

Native AirPrint / IPP printing for classic AmigaOS 3.0 and newer.

AmiAirPrint integrates network printers with the standard AmigaOS
printer.device system. It supports normal Amiga raster graphics and processed
text without CUPS, a PC print server, or a printer-specific classic driver.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.0 or newer
- Motorola 68000 or newer
- TCP/IP stack providing bsdsocket.library
- IPv4-reachable IPP/AirPrint printer

AmiAirPrint currently uses plain HTTP/IPP. TLS-only IPPS endpoints are not
supported.

Installation
------------

1. Start Install-AmiAirPrint with Installer 43.3.
2. Select AmigaOS 3.0 / 3.1 or AmigaOS 3.2+.
3. Select English (Built-in) or Deutsch.
4. Restart the Amiga.
5. In the normal Printer preferences select:

   Printer: AirPrint
   Port:    Parallel

6. Open SYS:Prefs/AmiAirPrint, discover or enter the printer, query it,
   choose the desired options and save.

Parallel is only a compatibility selection required by classic printer.device.
AmiAirPrint sends the actual print data directly through airprint.device.

Main features
-------------

- PWG Raster graphics printing through printer.device
- PDF and PostScript output when supported by the printer
- processed PRT:/CMD_WRITE text printing with Latin-1 support
- color and monochrome output
- Portrait and Landscape
- duplex long-edge / short-edge printing
- printer-reported media source / tray selection
- capability-based DPI selection
- paper/media, quality and color-mode selection
- 10-100% graphics scaling and optional centering
- Advanced print options in ReAction and GadTools preferences
- IPP printer capability query
- capability-aware full test page
- local printer discovery through mDNS/DNS-SD and SSDP
- locale.library support with built-in English fallback
- HTTP/IPP compatibility fallbacks for problematic printer firmware

Compatibility improvements in 1.2
---------------------------------

- FinalWriter striped graphics no longer cause endless blank pages.
- Wordworth multi-page graphics/form-feed handling is corrected.
- Multi-page and duplex PWG page boundaries are handled correctly.
- Broken Expect: 100-continue / HTTP 500 printer firmware has narrowly scoped
  compatibility handling without unsafe duplicate job retries.

Verified printing paths
-----------------------

- PersonalPaint color graphics
- MultiView graphics
- FinalWriter graphics
- Wordworth 5 multi-page graphics and duplex
- IBrowse processed text, including multi-page duplex
- repeated AmiAirPrint test pages

Component versions
------------------

Package / preferences: 1.2
AirPrint printer driver: 43.43
airprint.device: 1.2
Diagnostic tools: 1.2

Localization
------------

English is built into both preferences programs. The maintained German
translation source and AmiAirPrint.cd are supplied for CatComp, FlexCat or
compatible tools.

Known limitations
-----------------

- IPv4 only.
- TLS/IPPS is not implemented.
- IBrowse's classic printer path is text-only and may emit image ALT
  placeholders itself.
- PRD_RAWWRITE is not treated as portable text output.
- Normal WYSIWYG graphics remain raster-based even in PDF/PostScript output.
- printer.device uses exclusive access while an application keeps it open.

